WEBVTT

00:00:30.490 --> 00:00:33.760
Run at once towards a dream

00:00:30.490 --> 00:00:33.760
yume no mukou e ikkini hashitte yo

00:00:35.230 --> 00:00:38.730
Let’s meet and laugh away yesterday’s troubles

00:00:35.230 --> 00:00:38.730
nayameru kinou wo fungiri warai aou

00:00:40.070 --> 00:00:44.810
When our memories were here,

00:00:40.070 --> 00:00:44.810
omoide ga itta no toki mo

00:00:44.810 --> 00:00:47.030
even though we are deeply hurt, go straight on

00:00:44.810 --> 00:00:47.030
kizu wo fukai no ni massugu mae ni

00:00:47.030 --> 00:00:49.650
GO TO NEW WORLD

00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:54.420
I can feel it in the wind

00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:54.420
kaze no naka kanjiteru yo

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:58.080
The hot beat is shining

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:58.080
atsui kodou kagayaku yo

00:00:58.080 --> 00:01:00.560
especially now…

00:00:58.080 --> 00:01:00.560
ima koso

00:01:02.910 --> 00:01:07.500
surely, always, you’ll be by my side

00:01:02.910 --> 00:01:07.500
kitto zutto soba ni iru yo ne

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:12.360
Keep on running the way to the future.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:12.360
mirai no michi wo hashiri tsuzukeyou

00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:17.250
more and more, no matter what happens

00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:17.250
motto motto nani ga okitemo

00:01:17.250 --> 00:01:21.460
half our tears become double smiles

00:01:17.250 --> 00:01:21.460
namida wa hanbun nibai no egao ni naru

00:01:21.460 --> 00:01:24.010
forever

00:01:21.460 --> 00:01:24.010
itsudemo

00:01:33.950 --> 00:01:35.240
Isn’t this place all right?

00:01:36.300 --> 00:01:36.830
Huh?

00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:39.750
Habiko Detective Agency?

00:01:39.750 --> 00:01:42.600
Hold on, wasn’t that the place we went to earlier?

00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:43.700
Really?

00:01:44.300 --> 00:01:45.130
Then, how’s this…?

00:01:45.850 --> 00:01:47.950
Weren’t we there earlier, too?

00:01:48.670 --> 00:01:50.750
Geez… Are you taking this seriously?

00:01:51.700 --> 00:01:54.250
We don’t have much time.

00:01:54.250 --> 00:01:55.800
If we don’t find it quickly…

00:01:56.400 --> 00:01:57.800
Y-You’re right.

00:01:57.800 --> 00:01:58.520
Sorry.

00:02:02.650 --> 00:02:05.270
Futaba Detective Agency…

00:02:05.800 --> 00:02:09.110
Chief, Futaba Ainosuke…

00:02:09.750 --> 00:02:10.850
My dad is dead.

00:02:41.950 --> 00:02:43.400
Where is his son?

00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:46.200
Who knows? I haven’t seen him either.

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:48.000
He’s the only relative.

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:49.390
Just what is he thinking?

00:02:49.390 --> 00:02:52.450
Not even attending his father’s funeral…

00:02:52.450 --> 00:02:54.070
Young people these days…

00:03:03.350 --> 00:03:05.150
Farewell… dad.

00:03:16.150 --> 00:03:18.850
Oh yeah, wasn’t that expensive?

00:03:34.530 --> 00:03:36.700
Winter of 2002.

00:03:36.700 --> 00:03:38.900
So far, nothing much has changed.

00:03:39.850 --> 00:03:41.800
The same daily life,

00:03:41.800 --> 00:03:43.530
the same Christmas song,

00:03:44.050 --> 00:03:45.200
the same winter.

00:03:47.600 --> 00:03:49.350
Just that single thing was different…

00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:54.630
Traffic accident?

00:03:55.050 --> 00:03:56.400
Hey, it’s okay!

00:03:57.350 --> 00:03:58.930
We’ll play everyday.

00:03:59.300 --> 00:04:01.700
Anyway, what the hell are you doing?

00:04:01.700 --> 00:04:03.100
You’re disturbed.

00:04:02.230 --> 00:04:03.100
How scary…

00:04:04.350 --> 00:04:05.250
Really scary.

00:04:06.100 --> 00:04:07.560
What are you going to do?

00:04:13.300 --> 00:04:15.050
You don’t have to stop.

00:04:15.050 --> 00:04:16.350
It’s just a suspension…

00:04:20.300 --> 00:04:24.450
But you know, like, you forgot my birthday!

00:04:22.200 --> 00:04:23.600
Detective, huh…

00:04:24.450 --> 00:04:27.350
How many times did I already apologize for that?

00:04:27.350 --> 00:04:29.000
Give it a break!

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:29.500
It’s not bad.

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:32.600
Then, give me proof that you love me.

00:04:29.500 --> 00:04:32.600
It’d be cool to inherit your dad’s stuff, wouldn’t it?

00:04:32.600 --> 00:04:33.350
Proof?

00:04:33.350 --> 00:04:34.600
Kiss me now.

00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:34.600
What are you doing?

00:04:35.200 --> 00:04:36.710
Are you really gonna do it?

00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:39.400
UWAAH! Mikaru!

00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:41.400
Mikaru! He-Hey!!

00:04:41.400 --> 00:04:42.650
Hey, Rentarou!!

00:04:42.650 --> 00:04:43.600
Rentarou!

00:04:44.850 --> 00:04:48.000
That was my winter of 2002.

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:50.650
I was a violent college student,

00:04:50.650 --> 00:04:53.520
but not yet a violent detective.

00:04:57.050 --> 00:05:00.850
After I got suspended from college,

00:05:00.850 --> 00:05:04.160
everyone was talking about how I should follow in my old man’s footsteps.

00:05:07.000 --> 00:05:10.200
But, I had no plans to do so at all.

00:05:14.100 --> 00:05:16.150
It’s just that just about everything was a pain…

00:05:26.950 --> 00:05:28.100
And anything was all right…

00:05:30.350 --> 00:05:32.460
My dad frequently said something like this:

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:34.550
What are you going to do?

00:05:35.560 --> 00:05:38.000
Since I didn’t know what I should do…

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:40.500
For the time being, I watched the dusk in the winter of 2002.

00:05:57.550 --> 00:06:02.090
He’s singing the KareKano ending theme. But not very well.

00:06:06.150 --> 00:06:09.260
You should try and become an attractive man, like your father.

00:06:10.500 --> 00:06:12.680
They always said that.

00:06:25.800 --> 00:06:26.350
Hey…

00:06:27.900 --> 00:06:28.700
Hey…

00:06:30.200 --> 00:06:31.150
Hey!

00:06:31.150 --> 00:06:32.250
Ugh, yes!

00:06:33.650 --> 00:06:34.450
Ouch…

00:06:49.900 --> 00:06:52.800
Umm… can I help you with anything…?

00:06:53.450 --> 00:06:55.000
Anything, you say, This is…

00:06:55.000 --> 00:06:56.350
…a detective office,

00:06:56.350 --> 00:06:57.150
right?

00:06:57.150 --> 00:06:58.250
We wanted,

00:06:58.250 --> 00:06:59.250
to ask you,

00:06:59.250 --> 00:07:00.570
to do a job.

00:07:03.100 --> 00:07:03.650
What?

00:07:04.850 --> 00:07:06.950
This is the weather forecast for the Kanto region.

00:07:06.950 --> 00:07:12.250
Because of a low pressure front, the good weather will dissipate.

00:07:12.250 --> 00:07:15.850
Between evening and midnight, there’s a high probability of snowfall.

00:07:15.850 --> 00:07:19.650
Before going out, please be careful not to forget your umbrella.

00:07:19.650 --> 00:07:22.300
The snow will change to rain past midnight, and in the morning--

00:07:26.700 --> 00:07:27.050
Oh.

00:07:28.400 --> 00:07:31.930
Err… How much sugar do you want in your coffee?

00:07:37.450 --> 00:07:42.400
Umm, well… as I just said,
my old man just passed away.

00:07:42.400 --> 00:07:45.000
The business is closed for now…

00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:50.400
I’m sorry, but you’ll have to withdraw your request.

00:07:51.700 --> 00:07:53.200
Right now, you are

00:07:53.200 --> 00:07:54.400
the chief,

00:07:54.400 --> 00:07:55.450
right?

00:07:57.000 --> 00:07:59.600
Well… I wonder about that too…

00:08:00.850 --> 00:08:01.800
Are we wrong?

00:08:02.400 --> 00:08:04.250
Basically, I’m the successor…

00:08:04.250 --> 00:08:07.000
In case you forgot, Nidaime means “Second Generation.”

00:08:04.250 --> 00:08:07.000
I’m the indecisive and disgraceful Nidaime.

00:08:08.450 --> 00:08:11.590
Though, honestly, I don’t care much either way.

00:08:22.200 --> 00:08:23.150
Then…

00:08:23.150 --> 00:08:23.560
Huh?

00:08:24.100 --> 00:08:27.450
If you’re able to fulfill our request, you’ll take over the agency.

00:08:28.300 --> 00:08:30.150
If you’re not able to do it, you won’t.

00:08:34.350 --> 00:08:35.250
So?

00:08:50.400 --> 00:08:51.450
Accepted.

00:08:52.900 --> 00:08:54.970
From the beginning, Sara was like that.

00:08:56.050 --> 00:08:57.950
For example, like that time…

00:08:59.550 --> 00:09:04.550
The criminal is a militant who calls himself Dr. Ocean.

00:09:04.550 --> 00:09:06.800
Also, he’s armed with a machine gun.

00:09:06.800 --> 00:09:09.350
There are two civilian hostages inside the bathhouse.

00:09:09.350 --> 00:09:11.050
Requesting reinforcements from headquarters.

00:09:11.050 --> 00:09:13.800
Repeating, please answer!

00:09:13.800 --> 00:09:17.370
This is big news which will shock the world.

00:09:24.850 --> 00:09:26.300
I’m gonna kill you!

00:09:26.850 --> 00:09:28.300
What are you saying!!!

00:09:29.300 --> 00:09:31.010
Nothing at all!

00:09:31.900 --> 00:09:33.340
Comrades!

00:09:33.340 --> 00:09:39.250
The slack-jawed police are reporting that all the baths in the world have been taken over.

00:09:39.250 --> 00:09:43.520
There is only one place where I can perform this revolution, so I’m asking for your cooperation.

00:09:43.520 --> 00:09:46.000
If you don’t resist, I won’t hurt you.

00:09:47.940 --> 00:09:50.950
It really is too dangerous since he aimed his gun at us.

00:09:50.950 --> 00:09:51.600
Eh, what?

00:09:51.600 --> 00:09:53.650
Won’t your nakedness be completely exposed?

00:09:53.650 --> 00:09:59.250
If the television notices it, we won’t be able to become brides together!

00:09:59.250 --> 00:10:02.000
When that time comes, I’ll take responsibility.

00:10:05.250 --> 00:10:06.850
You’re so chatty!

00:10:06.850 --> 00:10:08.050
Even for a girl.

00:10:08.050 --> 00:10:08.750
That’s wro--

00:10:09.400 --> 00:10:11.800
S-Sorry, I couldn’t keep it in anymore.

00:10:12.800 --> 00:10:15.450
That guy thinks that there’s only the two of us here.

00:10:16.000 --> 00:10:16.900
Our chance will come!

00:10:17.310 --> 00:10:20.650
What’s happening here?

00:10:17.310 --> 00:10:18.950
Hey! You criminal!

00:10:18.950 --> 00:10:20.850
Get your ugly butt out here!

00:10:20.650 --> 00:10:22.700
I got called out by all the noise.

00:10:20.850 --> 00:10:23.500
Come out and show us how ugly you really are!

00:10:22.700 --> 00:10:27.000
Isn’t this all so exciting?

00:10:23.500 --> 00:10:28.050
HERE’S a big man for ya!

00:10:27.000 --> 00:10:30.050
That screaming is all so very loud…

00:10:28.050 --> 00:10:29.050
$@#*&%!@# o_o;

00:10:29.050 --> 00:10:30.050
SHUT UP!!!

00:10:30.050 --> 00:10:30.690
Waaaah!

00:10:31.950 --> 00:10:33.650
Listen up!

00:10:33.650 --> 00:10:37.150
The baths have been stolen by the slack-jawed police.

00:10:37.150 --> 00:10:41.550
I’ll brainwash the minds of 90% of the people’s mi--

00:10:41.550 --> 00:10:42.600
SHUT THE HELL UP!!!

00:10:42.600 --> 00:10:44.370
Be considerate of the people in the bathhouse!

00:10:44.550 --> 00:10:45.050
NOW!

00:10:51.650 --> 00:10:53.090
It’s an elephant!

00:10:53.090 --> 00:10:53.880
An elephant?

00:10:53.880 --> 00:10:55.380
DON’T SAY AN ELEPHANT!!!

00:10:55.850 --> 00:10:56.600
An opening!!!

00:11:09.900 --> 00:11:11.400
From the beginning, Sara was like that.

00:11:12.200 --> 00:11:14.350
Unlike those around her,
who did things hesitantly,

00:11:14.350 --> 00:11:17.200
she would always decide and do everything on her own.

00:11:17.200 --> 00:11:19.550
That sort of impulsive foolhardiness…

00:11:19.550 --> 00:11:24.100
How should I put it… am I envious, or am I not envious?

00:11:24.100 --> 00:11:27.250
Well, it’s pretty all right. Okay, okay!

00:11:27.250 --> 00:11:29.220
There might be some people who watched the television and will come to me with more work.

00:11:29.220 --> 00:11:30.220
I don’t know…

00:11:41.450 --> 00:11:42.720
W-What?

00:11:45.300 --> 00:11:46.730
Umm…

00:11:47.100 --> 00:11:48.400
Nothing at all.

00:12:04.700 --> 00:12:07.200
Aah, this is code, a code.

00:12:07.700 --> 00:12:08.660
A code?

00:12:09.150 --> 00:12:12.000
See here? It says that you should take out the “sa”.

00:12:12.000 --> 00:12:14.750
So take out the “sa” and then read the note.

00:12:14.750 --> 00:12:16.200
“The west entrance of the park…”

00:12:15.750 --> 00:12:17.950
Heh, you’re really like a detective.

00:12:18.650 --> 00:12:20.450
The detective is you, isn’t it?

00:12:21.400 --> 00:12:22.250
What?

00:12:22.250 --> 00:12:24.500
The detective is you, isn’t it?

00:12:26.050 --> 00:12:27.400
Wow.

00:12:27.400 --> 00:12:29.440
Are you okay?

00:12:29.850 --> 00:12:32.600
Well then, the detective is supposedly me.

00:12:45.000 --> 00:12:47.300
Darn it, geez!

00:12:49.600 --> 00:12:53.050
Head towards the west entrance.

00:12:54.350 --> 00:12:57.650
I went there, but there’s nothing here!

00:12:57.650 --> 00:13:00.600
THE HELL!

00:13:03.500 --> 00:13:04.180
Hm?

00:13:04.990 --> 00:13:07.200
We will be hiding somewhere in Futagotamagawa.

00:13:07.200 --> 00:13:10.900
If you can find us before 6p.m., we will pay the entire fee.

00:13:11.300 --> 00:13:13.190
Please search for us.

00:13:13.850 --> 00:13:17.480
To go searching all by myself, that’s not very funny at all.

00:13:20.550 --> 00:13:22.600
Playing hide and seek at this age?

00:13:30.200 --> 00:13:34.000
To begin with, I wonder why I went along with this game.

00:13:39.800 --> 00:13:40.750
It’s here!

00:13:44.400 --> 00:13:46.200
There’s nothing.

00:13:46.200 --> 00:13:47.400
That’s weird.

00:13:47.950 --> 00:13:49.300
Could you describe him more accurately…?

00:13:50.350 --> 00:13:53.400
Probably, it was because I didn’t know what to do.

00:13:54.150 --> 00:13:55.810
What are you going to do?

00:13:56.600 --> 00:14:00.850
But, I noticed that I was actually itching to make a move and do something.

00:14:01.750 --> 00:14:03.610
What are you going to do?

00:14:08.500 --> 00:14:10.120
You’re loitering around here…

00:14:10.120 --> 00:14:15.050
N-N-No-no-no-no! W-W-Wa-Wait, wait!

00:14:15.050 --> 00:14:16.900
In short, I thought that it was good to have this chance.

00:14:17.450 --> 00:14:18.420
What are you going to do?

00:14:30.350 --> 00:14:31.450
Err, wait--

00:14:31.450 --> 00:14:33.300
What am I going to do?

00:14:33.300 --> 00:14:35.000
That meat is huge!

00:14:35.000 --> 00:14:36.850
More importantly, how am I gonna get it?!

00:14:50.850 --> 00:14:52.350
What’s up with this Zippo!!

00:14:54.150 --> 00:14:55.850
Argh, I’m fed up!

00:14:56.600 --> 00:14:58.670
Aaaarrgghh!!

00:15:01.800 --> 00:15:03.150
I’ll stop.

00:15:04.150 --> 00:15:05.600
Thank you very much.

00:15:08.050 --> 00:15:09.350
HEY!

00:15:10.600 --> 00:15:12.450
Here, here! Hey!

00:15:18.250 --> 00:15:21.100
Thanks for taking care of things at the funeral.

00:15:22.000 --> 00:15:24.350
We’re all equals in times of trouble.

00:15:25.250 --> 00:15:28.070
It was bad enough that I didn’t go.

00:15:29.790 --> 00:15:34.080
I heard from Gen-san that you started your detective work.

00:15:34.080 --> 00:15:36.100
Ah… well.

00:15:34.080 --> 00:15:38.670
Red banner: Because we love this Nikotama

00:15:36.100 --> 00:15:38.300
That made me so happy!

00:15:38.300 --> 00:15:41.650
When he said that… You’re finally showing some motivation to do it.

00:15:43.000 --> 00:15:44.550
I’m going to stop.

00:15:44.550 --> 00:15:46.470
W-What?

00:15:47.350 --> 00:15:48.900
I have stopped, actually.

00:15:50.950 --> 00:15:51.750
I see.

00:15:52.650 --> 00:15:53.890
I’m sorry.

00:15:54.900 --> 00:15:55.800
I’m sorry.

00:15:58.500 --> 00:15:59.890
I’m sorry.

00:16:05.650 --> 00:16:06.500
Right.

00:16:06.500 --> 00:16:09.650
So I wonder what will happen now.

00:16:09.650 --> 00:16:12.850
All this is just an idea in his mind.

00:16:12.850 --> 00:16:15.400
I wonder if he’s going to pursue it though.

00:16:15.400 --> 00:16:18.200
Actually, it would take a lot of his skill.

00:16:20.450 --> 00:16:21.600
Well, it doesn’t matter.

00:16:21.600 --> 00:16:24.050
Since I wasn’t able to solve it, I won’t get paid.

00:16:24.050 --> 00:16:26.150
I wasn’t really into it from the start.

00:16:26.150 --> 00:16:28.250
Well, it doesn’t matter either way…

00:16:30.750 --> 00:16:32.800
Now let’s continue on to the next segment.

00:16:33.550 --> 00:16:36.220
I’m so… uncool.

00:16:37.050 --> 00:16:39.200
You shouldn’t stop!

00:16:39.200 --> 00:16:42.000
You are you. Ai-san is Ai-san.

00:16:42.000 --> 00:16:46.200
It may be that the people around you are too insensitive, including me.

00:16:46.200 --> 00:16:47.170
In the end,

00:16:47.170 --> 00:16:51.000
it doesn’t matter who is replacing whom.

00:17:04.300 --> 00:17:09.260
This is an old japanese children’s song.

00:17:31.070 --> 00:17:32.900
Hey, hey, hey, hey!

00:17:33.850 --> 00:17:35.300
What is this?!

00:17:38.350 --> 00:17:39.850
What is going on with me?!?!

00:17:40.900 --> 00:17:43.450
Even needed some 12 years old brats for me to notice it!

00:17:45.090 --> 00:17:47.000
How pathetic, pathetic, PATHETIC!

00:17:49.750 --> 00:17:51.750
Who am I?

00:17:51.750 --> 00:17:53.010
Who am I…?

00:17:54.150 --> 00:17:55.760
I’M FUTABA RENTAROU!

00:17:58.800 --> 00:18:02.950
Well, I already know that you are Futaba Rentarou, but..

00:18:02.950 --> 00:18:07.450
I am not willing to lend you my bike.

00:18:07.450 --> 00:18:09.650
Where do you want to go in all this rain?

00:18:09.650 --> 00:18:10.650
Hey, Rentarou?

00:18:10.650 --> 00:18:11.150
Rentarou!

00:18:11.550 --> 00:18:12.200
Hey!

00:18:26.100 --> 00:18:29.460
Futaba Rentarou, heading off
to solve his first case.

00:18:32.450 --> 00:18:34.050
Yup, get going!

00:18:34.680 --> 00:18:36.150
Nidaime!

00:18:37.450 --> 00:18:39.100
What are you going to do?

00:18:39.700 --> 00:18:46.150
I still don’t know about that, but… for now, I’m hell-bent on fighting that dog!

00:18:46.700 --> 00:18:48.310
From the beginning, Soujyu was like that.

00:18:48.750 --> 00:18:50.950
In the event that you couldn’t find us,

00:18:50.950 --> 00:18:53.550
we have put the money inside the post box.

00:18:53.550 --> 00:18:55.800
Thank you for having been with us.

00:18:55.800 --> 00:18:58.350
Please work hard at your detective work.

00:18:59.400 --> 00:19:03.950
Running away while smiling gently and always thinking about someone else.

00:19:08.100 --> 00:19:09.250
ATTACK!

00:19:22.200 --> 00:19:23.900
Shall we go home, Sara-chan?

00:19:26.550 --> 00:19:30.000
He surely has been searching with all his might,

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:33.270
but since the hints were a bit too difficult, he might not have been able to find us.

00:19:33.750 --> 00:19:36.550
Next time, let’s make some easier ones, okay?

00:19:38.850 --> 00:19:43.160
It can’t be helped; we only just met him today after all.

00:19:43.160 --> 00:19:46.670
And this stuff would probably be meaningless to him.

00:19:47.300 --> 00:19:48.350
He wouldn’t find us--

00:19:48.350 --> 00:19:49.460
I don’t want to…

00:19:49.950 --> 00:19:51.300
I don’t want to go back!!

00:19:52.150 --> 00:19:55.350
I was afraid the whole time in that pitch-black darkness.

00:19:55.350 --> 00:19:57.300
I couldn’t do anything,
no matter what I decided!

00:19:57.700 --> 00:19:58.900
Sara-chan…

00:19:58.900 --> 00:19:59.750
We…

00:19:59.750 --> 00:20:02.750
Isn’t it good if we can decide our future by ourselves??

00:20:06.150 --> 00:20:06.900
The rain…

00:20:09.400 --> 00:20:10.160
… stopped.

00:20:34.530 --> 00:20:39.450
FOUND YOU!!!

00:21:06.750 --> 00:21:08.000
U-Umm…

00:21:17.650 --> 00:21:18.900
Caught you.

00:21:19.650 --> 00:21:21.670
Also, thank you.

00:21:22.300 --> 00:21:25.000
Thanks to you guys, I managed to do it somehow. Yeah…

00:21:34.300 --> 00:21:35.910
We got caught.

00:21:38.400 --> 00:21:39.850
The same daily life,

00:21:40.500 --> 00:21:42.050
the same Christmas song,

00:21:43.300 --> 00:21:45.440
the same winter.

00:21:49.250 --> 00:21:54.080
The violent college student became a violent detective.

00:21:58.300 --> 00:22:00.310
Don’t cry… okay?

00:22:02.400 --> 00:22:03.900
Nothing much has changed.

00:22:16.500 --> 00:22:18.800
It’s changed just a little.

00:22:20.150 --> 00:22:25.800
We are here.

00:22:20.150 --> 00:22:25.630
bokura wa koko ni iru

00:22:26.130 --> 00:22:33.200
We will be here.

00:22:26.130 --> 00:22:33.200
bokura ga koko ni aru

00:22:33.580 --> 00:22:38.520
The slow time is

00:22:33.580 --> 00:22:38.520
yuruyaka na jikan ga

00:22:38.830 --> 00:22:45.450
flowing in this room.

00:22:38.830 --> 00:22:45.450
nagareteru kono heya de

00:22:46.130 --> 00:22:49.050
Even if the summer days vanish,

00:22:46.130 --> 00:22:49.050
natsu no hi ga kiete mo

00:22:49.280 --> 00:22:53.110
the smiles that remain

00:22:49.280 --> 00:22:53.110
nokoru egao tachi

00:22:53.230 --> 00:22:59.990
are a chain of happiness up to this point.

00:22:53.230 --> 00:22:59.990
kocchi made shiawase no rensa

00:23:00.260 --> 00:23:05.830
Ah, the meaning of honesty,

00:23:00.260 --> 00:23:05.830
aa sunaosa no imi

00:23:06.140 --> 00:23:14.170
is within the innermost depths of your heart.

00:23:06.140 --> 00:23:14.170
KOKORO no zutto zutto oku no hou e

00:23:14.440 --> 00:23:19.550
Hey, the days are wonderful

00:23:14.440 --> 00:23:19.550
nee subarashii hibi

00:23:19.850 --> 00:23:27.310
in the midst of weakness and anxiety.

00:23:19.850 --> 00:23:27.310
yowasa to fuan no naka de shitte

00:23:27.380 --> 00:23:33.860
I won’t say goodbye, Because forever

00:23:27.380 --> 00:23:33.860
sayonara wa iwanai yo datte itsumademo

00:23:34.050 --> 00:23:39.140
the days will be unchanged.

00:23:34.050 --> 00:23:39.140
kawaru koto no nai hibi

00:23:39.330 --> 00:23:45.980
Surely forever. M

00:23:39.330 --> 00:23:45.980
kitto itsumademo

